## Unimplemented Requirements

User requirements we did not have time to implement:


- **REQ-STUDENT-2**: A student needs the instructions to be simple, so they can understand them even with limited knowledge of Swedish.
  - **REQ-STUDENT-2.1**: Instructions shall use short sentences and vocabulary already covered in the course. *(Requires user testing with students.)*

- **REQ-TEACHER-5**: A teacher needs the game to be available to students with different accessibility requirements, so that all students can use the game.
  - **REQ-TEACHER-5.1**: The system shall provide options that allow students with different requirements to interact with the game.

- **REQ-DEVELOPER-7**: A future developer needs a way to test the game logic, so changes can be verified without manually checking everything by hand.
  - **REQ-DEVELOPER-7.1**: The system shall include an automated test suite that verifies the game logic and can be run with a single command.
  - **REQ-DEVELOPER-7.2**: The system shall report the result of each test run as pass or fail per test, with a message that identifies which test failed and why, so a developer can locate the problem without manual checking.

- **REQ-STUDENT-20**: A student needs the game to render and function consistently across common web browsers (e.g. Chrome, Firefox, Safari), so that all students have a reliable experience regardless of which browser they use. *(This should probably work, but it has not been thoroughly tested.)*

- **REQ-STUDENT-22**: A student needs to be able to get help when stuck in the game, so the student does not give up.
  - **REQ-STUDENT-22.1**: Add language hints.

### Other implementations to follow up on
- Hide the scrollbars that are in the wardrobe.
- Replace the "Back to level-selecting-page" button with a clearer "Back to menu" button.